-- Demo data for local and staging environments (never production). Enabled by adding classpath:db/seed-demo to
-- APP_FLYWAY_LOCATIONS after classpath:db/seed-dev, whose users (ids 1-4) it references.
--
-- Why a repeatable migration: Flyway applies versioned migrations in numeric order, so a versioned seed would run
-- before (or block) the timestamped schema migrations that create the tables it fills. A repeatable migration always
-- runs after every versioned one, so future schema migrations never break it.
--
-- Rules that keep it safe to re-run (Flyway re-applies it whenever this file changes):
--   * Fixed ids in reserved ranges, inserted with "ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE <key> = <key>": rows that already exist are
--     left untouched (any other error still fails the migration). Users 101+, locations 101+, requests 1001+,
--     history 10001+, comments 20001+, notifications 30001+, triage rules 101+.
--   * Request codes are assigned after the rows exist, continuing request_code_sequences, so they never collide with
--     codes already issued and the application keeps numbering after the last one.
--   * Timestamps are relative to the moment the script runs (stored as UTC, office hours in Lima), so the dashboards
--     always show recent activity. To refresh them, recreate the database (docker compose ... down -v).
--   * Requests in RESUELTA were resolved less than 72 hours before the script runs: they stay pending confirmation
--     until the automatic closure (system_settings.auto_close_hours) closes them as real ones would be.
--
-- DemoSeedTests checks the data after any edit: every request follows the state machine of the workflow module (same
-- history texts), deadlines follow the SLA, codes continue the sequence and re-running the script changes nothing.
-- Evidences are not seeded because their files would not exist in the storage volume.

SET @now = UTC_TIMESTAMP(6);
-- Midnight of the current day in Lima (UTC-5, no daylight saving), expressed in UTC.
SET @today = TIMESTAMP(DATE(@now - INTERVAL 5 HOUR), '05:00:00');

-- Demo users (password Demo12345!) besides the four of db/seed-dev.
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE id = id;

-- More rooms, so requests spread over several pavilions.
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE id = id;

